    ('p', 'Routing is a pure function of the task policy, the payload, and the live state of providers and budget - no LLM decides routing, and no stage knows providers exist. The decision procedure runs per task, in order: (1) policy tier - local-fixed tasks stop here; (2) payload fit - if input exceeds the local model context window or minContextChars, escalate; (3) budget - cloud is allowed only if the ledger has headroom (hard stop otherwise); (4) provider health - skip providers marked unhealthy in the last 15 minutes; (5) preference order from models.yaml. The retry ladder for a failed attempt is exactly: repair-retry once on the same provider (schema failures only), then escalate one step up the preference chain, then mark the task failed with errorCode and surface it per Table 3.6. Cloud-to-cloud fallback counts against the same ladder.'),
