    ('p', 'Call detail (4) is the app\'s center of gravity and uses a fixed scaffold: a 56px header strip (title, deal chip, stage rail with six pips, actions), then a tab body. The stage rail is the state machine made visible - pips for UPLOADED through READY light progressively amber, the active stage pulses gently, and a FAILED pip turns danger-red with a retry affordance on hover. Overview tab is a 12-column grid: summary card full-width, then MEDDIC six-pack (2x3 cards, each with value-or-NOT_FOUND, confidence dots, evidence links), risk flags row, metrics row (talk ratio dial, questions, monologue), then notes and follow-up side by side. Evidence links everywhere open the transcript reader scrolled to the segment with a soft highlight pulse - this single interaction is the most-used in the app and gets a 200ms ease, not an instant jump.'),
    ('p', 'Pipeline board (7) renders stage columns LEAD through WON/LOST with PARKED collapsed to a rail; cards show account, title, value, health dot (green/amber/red by 66/33 cutoffs), and up to two risk badges. Drag uses a warm ghost (accent-soft, 90% scale); drop updates optimistically and reconciles with the PATCH response. Deal detail (8) leads with the health gauge and stage stepper, then the MEDDIC completeness panel (six cells, filled cells in accent-soft), the auto-built timeline down the left column, contacts with champion/EB flags on the right, and the deal\'s calls as compact rows. Scorecard detail (11) shows six dimension cards (score dial, evidence links, coach comment) with the weighted overall on top and a compare toggle overlaying your top-quartile means as ghost markers. Settings - Providers (15) is one card per adapter: status pill (live health), model dropdown sourced from models.yaml, latency of the last test, and a test button whose result animates in place.'),
